//
// GAME TYPE = which world/game-experience (vanilla, skyblock, prison, ...).
// Each one gets its own ISOLATED, persistent world — switching types never
// touches another type's saved world again. Mechanically: every type maps to
// its own itzg `LEVEL` value (the sanitized type key itself), so its world
// lives in its own `<LEVEL>`/`<LEVEL>_nether`/`<LEVEL>_the_end` folder set
// inside the SAME /data volume mount (see recreateGameTypeContainer below).
// This directly fixes the production incident where a SkyBlock->Vanilla
// switch corrupted the one shared world.
//
// GAME MODE = survival/hardcore/creative/peaceful, a lightweight
// server.properties overlay (gamemode/hardcore/difficulty) applied WITHIN
// whichever type is currently active, via RCON + a restart of the SAME
// container — no world switch, no recreate, no LEVEL change.
//
// LEVEL behavior confirmed LIVE against freemc-host before writing any of the
// code that depends on it (2026-08-25):
//   - Two containers on the SAME /data volume, `-e LEVEL=testmodeA` and
//     `-e LEVEL=testmodeB`, each produced their own `<LEVEL>`/`<LEVEL>_nether`/
//     `<LEVEL>_the_end` folder set; neither boot touched the other's files.
//   - A Paper container with `-e LEVEL=skyblock` created `skyblock`/
//     `skyblock_nether`/`skyblock_the_end` as its BASE world (confirmed via
//     `ServerLevel[skyblock]` in the boot log), exactly like the vanilla case.
//   - HOWEVER: IridiumSkyblock's own custom dimensions do NOT follow LEVEL —
//     they are always named `iridiumskyblock`/`iridiumskyblock_nether`/
//     `iridiumskyblock_the_end` regardless of the LEVEL value (the plugin
//     hardcodes its own world name). That's harmless for isolation ACROSS
//     accounts (every account has its own /data volume) and across OTHER game
//     types on the same account (no other type here uses IridiumSkyblock), but
//     it means deleteFreeMinecraftWorld must remove these explicitly too, not
//     just glob `<LEVEL>*` — see `extraWorldFolders` below.
//   - Restarting the SAME container (a MODE change) never touched any world
